{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:103494",
  "title": "Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-26 12:18:59"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-28 06:08:02"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: net: sit: require CAP_NET_ADMIN in the device netns for changelink (CVE-2026-72061)\n\n* kernel: KVM: Move kvm_io_bus_get_dev() locking responsibilities to callers (CVE-2026-72282)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-tcp: check return value of nvmet_tcp_set_queue_sock (CVE-2026-74385)\n\n* kernel: iommu/tegra241-cmdqv: Reject a vSID wider than the SID_MATCH field (CVE-2026-89450)\n\n* kernel: iommu/tegra241-cmdqv: Synchronize the error ISR against VINTF (de)init (CVE-2026-90429)\n\n* kernel: vdpa_sim_blk: reject out-of-range sector starts (CVE-2026-97991)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Use-after-free via race condition in memory folio truncation (CVE-2026-99462)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* kvm: aarch64 CVE backport CW46 (JIRA:Rocky Linux-305162)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
